# Exposed UI

Import components and public types from the `src/lib/ui/index.ts` barrel (for example `./lib/ui` from `src/Example.svelte`). Load `../lib/ui/styles.css` once in `src/routes/+layout.svelte`. It includes tokens, actions, patterns, focus rings, hidden captions, highlighted text and animation prerequisites. Field and Notice keep scoped styles. `/design-system` is the interactive reference in development only and requires no declarations API. Production returns 404 and hides its footer link.

Features own amounts, availability, chart geometry, URLs, analytics and async work. UI accepts formatted strings and presentation models. Pages own grids and section spacing. Use the [composition recipes](COMPOSITION.md) for native rows, declarations and identities.

| Component                              | Contract                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |
| -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Button, ButtonLink                     | `variant` primary/secondary/quiet/subtle; `size` regular/large/compact/inline. Native attributes and handlers pass through. Button defaults to `type="button"`; links require `href`.                                                |
| Field                                  | Required visible `label`; `type` text/search/date; bindable string `value`; `defaultValue` supports native reset. `hint` and `error` join caller `aria-describedby`. Native attributes reach the input; `class` reaches the wrapper. |
| SearchField                            | Required `label`, `help` snippet and `onclear`; bindable string `value` and native `input` reference; optional `shortcut`. Native attributes including `class` reach the input. Caller owns query behavior and focus restoration.    |
| Notice                                 | `tone` neutral/accent/warning. Native div attributes pass through. Caller chooses announcement `role`.                                                                                                                               |
| Badge                                  | `variant` result (default), profile or legend. `class` adds a root hook without replacing appearance.                                                                                                                                |
| MessageState                           | Required `title`; `variant` centered (default) or detail; `level` 1/2 changes semantics independently of appearance. Optional `icon`, `children`, `actions`, `role`, additive root `class`.                                          |
| SectionHeading                         | Required `id`, `title`; optional `level` 1/2/3 and trailing children. Heading presentation stays independent of rank.                                                                                                                |
| Disclosure                             | Required `summary`, children; `variant` names (default) or plain. Native details attributes, additive root `class`, bindable `open`.                                                                                                 |
| Metric                                 | Required `label`, formatted `value`; optional `regionLabel`, `available`, `description`, `level` 2/3. `variant` default or expanded. Available values remain keyboard-scrollable regions; unavailable text remains ordinary text.    |
| DeclarationCard                        | Required `heading`, `registered`, children snippets. `variant` default or compact changes padding.                                                                                                                                   |
| ValueRow                               | Required `source` and `value` snippets. Owns its `li` layout, including outside `.funding-list`; nested lists retain native layout.                                                                                                  |
| DataTable                              | Required text `caption`, `head` snippet and body children. Callers supply native rows, cells, scope and column-specific classes. No numeric alignment or column widths are assumed.                                                  |
| IdentityHeader                         | Required `name`, `kind`, `metadata`; optional `values`, `navigation`, `level` 1/2/3.                                                                                                                                                 |
| ResultRow, DeclarationList             | Native `li` and `ol` wrappers; children and optional accessible `label`. ResultRow callers supply their own anchor and may add a root `class` for a local palette.                                                                   |
| SignedBarList                          | `bars: SignedBar[]`, `baseline`; `variant` default or compact. Values are formatted strings; widths and signs come from features.                                                                                                    |
| BarChart, PieChart                     | Typed `ChartBar[]` geometry and `PieSlice[]` presentation data. Features calculate shares, signs and totals. See [RegistrationTimeline](../../RegistrationTimeline.svelte) and [FunderSummary](../../FunderSummary.svelte).          |
| ViewLinks, ViewLink, Pagination        | Native navigation. Callers own destinations/current page; Pagination owns bound availability.                                                                                                                                        |
| Icon, IconIndicator                    | Canonical `IconName`; Icon is decorative. IconIndicator owns focus, pointer and Escape hints.                                                                                                                                        |
| HighlightedText, Spinner, SkeletonRows | Literal text highlights and decorative progress.                                                                                                                                                                                     |

Classes on native-attribute components accept Svelte class arrays and objects. Where a structural component exposes `class`, it adds a root hook. No class replacement API is supported. Use finite variants for existing appearances; caller-authored snippet classes own feature text and arrangements. The recipes show those classes explicitly.

Tokens in [tokens.css](tokens.css) own colors, spacing, type and focus. The browser’s light/dark preference selects the palette through CSS and updates the current page automatically. Native fields inherit that scheme. Keep accent-derived mixes on component selectors so local entity overrides resolve there; root tokens supply palette endpoints and mix proportions. Override `--accent` on a container for another palette, such as `var(--accent-funder)`. Result indicators, badges and highlights derive their colors from the local accent; a ResultRow root `class` can select that palette explicitly. `--focus-width` and `--focus-offset` apply at the root or on a container. Native links, buttons and summaries add one pixel to the offset. Do not import internal stylesheets individually.

The [barrel](index.ts) is the public inventory. The gallery covers native disclosure/input behavior, precise metric overflow, repeated association IDs and pointer tooltip lifecycle. Financial parsing and availability decisions belong in feature adapters, never in UI components.

UI-owned snippet classes are `.results-list` (list reset and divider), `.entity-text` (shrinkable content), `.entity-name` (result anchor typography and hover), `.entity-alias` (secondary result text), `.funding-list` (nested list reset and spacing), `.declaration-reference`, `.payment-type`, `.currency-label`, `.empty-entry` (declaration context), `.amount` (exact value typography), and `.entry-count`/`.partial-note` (secondary chart/table text). These work with the single UI stylesheet import. Feature grids and custom table columns stay in callers.
# Light mode design

The browser owns the effective light or dark scheme. The design system token file owns the palette. Components retain their existing props and use semantic colors. CSS media queries select the light palette without JavaScript, persistence, or a theme controller.

Use the Sol candidate as the base for its complete migration and verification plan. Graft Astra’s component-local accent derivation rule so funder teal cannot resolve to root purple. Graft the gallery live swatch refresh from Sol. Explicit theme state from Luna is rejected because no script consumer or manual override needs it. Media queries preserve dark defaults more clearly than light-dark().

Appearance roles cover surfaces, controls, hover/focus, borders, text, skeletons, tooltips, chart remainder, selection, and footer. Keep existing dark values where possible. Light mode uses a restrained lavender canvas with dark purple/teal accents. Party category colors and financial behavior remain owned by existing feature code.

app.html provides a media-aware initial canvas and browser metadata. Verify its small duplication against resolved CSS values. Native fields inherit color-scheme. Derived local accent expressions stay on component selectors.

Verification requires check/build, existing affected browser tests, meaningful theme behavior tests, desktop screenshots and direct screenshot inspection. Cover system preference changes, JavaScript-disabled first paint, native dates, text contrast, control boundaries, both entity palettes, primary hover, tooltip, loading/empty/error and charts.

Candidate rubric scores, each out of 5. Sol 5/5/5/5/5. Astra 5/5/5/5/5. Luna 4/3/3/4/4. Sol provides the fuller integration plan; Astra supplies the essential local-accent warning. Independent Luna judge agrees with Sol base plus Astra local-accent rule.
### Feature

**You own the design. Plan, review, verify.** Delegate implementation. Stay in the lead.

1. `how` over the affected subsystem.
2. `architect` for parallel design exploration.
3. Write the throughput checkpoint as four todo items. A dimension that genuinely does not apply (single file, no fan-out) keeps its item with `n/a: <reason>` rather than being dropped:
   - **Blocking first steps.** Gates run before fan-out.
   - **Independent workstreams.** Disjoint files, services, or layers parallelize. Shared writes serialize.
   - **Shared mutable state.** Default to splitting the target (the **separate-before-serializing-shared-state** principle skill). Serialize only for real invariants.
   - **Smallest safe decomposition.** If one worker is best, name why.
4. Delegate code-writing to a subagent using your configured feature model (default in poteto-mode's Models section) with a specific scope (file paths, named data shape and its organizing structure per **principle-model-the-domain**, a state machine over scattered booleans, a table/registry over branching, a typed model over repeated shape assumptions, chosen before the delegate writes logic, and success criteria). Pick each subagent's reasoning level for the job, per the Subagents section. When the implementation admits multiple valid shapes (error handling, abstraction layer, test structure), delegate via the **arena** skill instead so the runners surface the alternatives and the cross-judge guards the pick. Mandatory: no skip-with-reason escape, and Laziness Protocol does not override it (the gain is review separation, not lines saved). A subagent forbidden to spawn satisfies this by owning the diff directly with the same review separation. No "standing by" reply that waits on a nested agent. **Give every file-writing delegate its own worktree** (spawn it with `isolation: "worktree"`, or hand it an exclusive branch), and do not write files or run a suite in a worktree a delegate still holds. On Claude Code, `isolation: "worktree"` branches from the remote default branch unless the `worktree.baseRef` setting is `"head"`. When the delegate builds on commits the default branch lacks, commit them, create its worktree with `git worktree add <path> -b <delegate-branch> HEAD`, and name that base commit in the brief. Fencing a file in the brief's prose is not a lock (**principle-separate-before-serializing-shared-state**). Comments per **Comments**. Surgical edits, re-ground against the source for upstream-derived files. Port shared-primitive improvements to all consumers and verify each. Commit liberally.
5. Verify on the matching surface. "Inconclusive" or wrong-surface is not a pass. Flag it.
6. Rebase into small, ordered commits. Stack follow-ups.
   Use the **sequence-verifiable-units** principle skill, building, verifying, and committing each small unit before the next.
7. If the design is contested, `interrogate` before shipping.
8. Run **Opening a PR**.

Code-coupled work (one feature, one migration) goes to a single owner with the checkpoint inline. That owner fans out internally after the blocking phase. Parent-level fan-out is for slices that produce independent artifacts (audits, cross-subsystem investigations, competing experiments). Rewrite the checkpoint at phase boundaries. Spawn a fresh owner rather than chaining interrupts.

**Reply:** what you built, what you chose and why, the throughput checkpoint, open decisions. Tables for design alternatives.

## Throughput checkpoint
- Blocking first steps. Inspect merged design system and compare theme ownership designs before implementation.
- Independent workstreams. Read-only design candidates run in parallel; one owner implements shared tokens and consumers.
- Shared mutable state. Each design candidate writes only its own /tmp artifact. One exclusive implementation worktree.
- Smallest safe decomposition. One implementation owner because tokens, inline first paint, and component colors must change together.

## Phases
- [x] Ground / how.
- [x] Sketch / arena frame, fan out, cross-judge, pick, graft.
- [x] Agree. Proceed with default system preference.
- [x] Implement.
- [x] Scrap if needed. n/a: selected CSS design satisfied verification.
- [ ] Verify / screenshots / independent review. Implementation checks/build and 94 affected tests passed; 10 desktop captures viewed. Independent review remains with root.
- [ ] Deslop / no-comments / commit / open PR.

Implementation deslop and technical-writing passes complete. No application comments or runtime theme controller added. Commit and PR remain with root.
